  ($q$cs-497$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$Although the new policy was intended to be ______, many employees found the rules so complicated that they needed weeks to understand them.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["expensive","controversial","straightforward","temporary"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The word "Although" signals a contrast: the policy was meant to be easy to follow, but employees found it complicated. "Straightforward" fits.$q$),
  ($q$cs-498$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Standardized time zones were adopted mainly to serve the needs of railroads.

Text 2: Railroads were a driving force, but telegraph companies, which also needed coordinated time, deserve equal credit.$q$, $q$Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the claim in Text 1?$q$, $q$["By claiming that telegraphs were irrelevant to timekeeping","By denying that railroads influenced time zones","By arguing that time zones were not standardized","By acknowledging the role of railroads while adding another contributing factor"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Text 2 accepts the railroads' role yet adds the telegraph companies as equally important.$q$),
  ($q$cs-499$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 1, $q$Pioneering aviator Bessie Coleman was denied entry to American flight schools because she was Black and a woman. Undeterred, she learned French and moved to France, where she earned her pilot's license in 1921. Her determination opened the door for generations of aviators who followed.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?$q$, $q$["It provides a counterexample to the claim made in the first sentence.","It shows how the figure responded to the obstacle described in the first sentence.","It introduces a new topic unrelated to the first sentence.","It restates the first sentence in more detail."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$After the obstacle in sentence one, sentence two describes how Coleman overcame it.$q$),
  ($q$cs-500$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The ambassador's ______ manner put both parties at ease, allowing negotiations to resume.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["conciliatory","impatient","aloof","combative"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$A manner that eases tension between rivals is "conciliatory."$q$),
  ($q$cs-501$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The professor's lectures were ______ rather than dry; students often stayed after class to continue discussing the topics.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["lengthy","confusing","monotonous","engaging"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Students wanting to continue discussing shows the lectures held their interest, in contrast to "dry": "engaging."$q$),
  ($q$cs-502$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: The fossil record shows that mass extinctions are followed by rapid diversification of surviving species.

Text 2: Diversification after an extinction is not always rapid; in several documented cases, recovery took millions of years.$q$, $q$Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the claim in Text 1?$q$, $q$["By denying that mass extinctions have occurred","By agreeing that diversification is always rapid","By arguing that the fossil record is too incomplete to study","By qualifying the claim with cases in which recovery was slow"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Text 2 does not reject Text 1 but notes exceptions in which recovery was slow.$q$),
  ($q$cs-503$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$In "Ode to a Teacup," the speaker transforms a humble object into a source of wonder, comparing its curve to the horizon of a small planet. Critics note that this elevation of the ordinary is typical of the poet's work, which often finds grandeur in domestic objects.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall purpose of the text?$q$, $q$["To argue that domestic objects are unsuitable subjects for poetry","To describe a poem's approach and relate it to a broader pattern in the poet's work","To compare two poems by different authors","To explain how teacups are manufactured"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The text describes what the poem does and then notes that this is typical of the poet's approach.$q$),
  ($q$cs-504$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: The fall of the Western Roman Empire was caused chiefly by foreign invasion.

Text 2: Invasions mattered, but internal economic decline had already weakened the empire's ability to resist them.$q$, $q$Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the claim in Text 1?$q$, $q$["By arguing that the empire never actually fell","By denying that any invasions took place","By agreeing that invasions played a role but arguing that they were not the whole explanation","By claiming that economic decline was caused by the invasions"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Text 2 accepts the role of invasions yet adds economic decline as a deeper cause.$q$),
  ($q$cs-505$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$Critics found the sequel ______, complaining that it merely repeated the plot of the original without adding anything new.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["brief","innovative","ambitious","derivative"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$A work that only repeats an earlier one is "derivative."$q$),
  ($q$cs-506$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$To reduce the risk of ______, the lab requires researchers to label and date all samples.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["confusion","expansion","boredom","competition"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Labeling and dating samples helps researchers keep them straight and avoid mix-ups: "confusion."$q$),
  ($q$cs-507$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The engineer's proposal was ______ by budget constraints; the design was sound, but the city could not afford it.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["thwarted","strengthened","inspired","clarified"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The design was good but unaffordable, so the proposal was blocked: "thwarted."$q$),
  ($q$cs-508$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The company's ______ approach to hiring, considering only résumés and never interviewing, meant that talented candidates were sometimes overlooked.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["generous","flexible","rigid","inclusive"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Refusing to consider anything beyond résumés is an inflexible, "rigid" approach.$q$),
  ($q$cs-509$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$Because the soil in the region is naturally ______, farmers there must add nutrients each season to grow healthy crops.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["fertile","uniform","expansive","infertile"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Farmers must add nutrients because the soil lacks them on its own, i.e., it is "infertile."$q$),
