  ($q$cs-528$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The botanist's meticulous notes were ______ to later researchers, who relied on them to rediscover plants not seen in a century.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["misleading","invaluable","redundant","irrelevant"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Researchers relied on the notes to make a rediscovery, so the notes were extremely useful: "invaluable."$q$),
  ($q$cs-529$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$Researchers studying urban noise placed sensors at 40 intersections over six months. They found that average sound levels exceeded the World Health Organization's recommended limit at 31 of the sites. The team recommends that cities consider lowering speed limits and installing sound barriers near homes.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It explains how sound sensors are manufactured.","It compares noise levels in cities with those in rural areas.","It describes a study's method, reports its main result, and presents recommendations based on that result.","It presents a theory, tests it, and abandons it."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The sentences move from method to finding to recommendation.$q$),
  ($q$cs-530$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$The mathematician Emmy Noether, whose work underpins much of modern physics, taught for years without pay because German universities would not appoint women to professorships. Her colleagues David Hilbert and Felix Klein championed her cause, arguing that a candidate's sex was no argument against admission. Still, she did not receive a paid position until 1923.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It compares the teaching styles of three mathematicians.","It describes obstacles faced by a scholar, mentions efforts to overcome them, and notes their limited success.","It argues that universities should have hired more mathematicians.","It summarizes Noether's major scientific discoveries in chronological order."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The text presents the barrier (no paid appointment), the allies who pushed back, and the late result ("Still...").$q$),
  ($q$cs-531$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 1, $q$The two committees, though ______ in their goals, differed sharply about the best methods for achieving them.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["united","indifferent","uncertain","opposed"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$"Though" and "differed sharply about methods" indicate that the committees agreed about goals: "united."$q$),
